1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,741
Ava: A 3.6-billion-parameter robot policy ran on an 8 GB Jetson Orin Nano with ExecuTorch-TensorRT.
Ava：一个拥有 36 亿参数的机器人策略通过 ExecuTorch-TensorRT，在 8 GB 的 Jetson Orin Nano 上运行。

2
00:00:08,741 --> 00:00:13,483
PyTorch eager mode ran out of memory on that board.
PyTorch 即时执行模式在这块板子上内存不足。

3
00:00:13,483 --> 00:00:18,110
The measured time was 467 ms per action chunk.
实测每个动作块耗时 467 毫秒。

4
00:00:18,110 --> 00:00:23,643
Brian: That matters because a policy produces a short plan, called an action chunk.
Brian：这很关键，因为策略会生成一段短期计划，称为动作块。

5
00:00:23,643 --> 00:00:29,467
If the next chunk isn't ready when the robot finishes the current one, it waits.
如果机器人执行完当前动作块时，下一个还没准备好，就得等待。

6
00:00:29,467 --> 00:00:35,860
Sending the work to a server adds a network round trip that can easily take 100 ms.
把计算交给服务器会增加一次网络往返，耗时很容易达到 100 毫秒。

7
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:43,760
Ava: TensorRT is fast on NVIDIA hardware, but getting a PyTorch model there has been awkward.
Ava：TensorRT 在 NVIDIA 硬件上很快，但把 PyTorch 模型转过去一直不太方便。

8
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:53,635
With ONNX-TensorRT, the model has to pass through both the PyTorch ONNX exporter and the TensorRT ONNX parser.
用 ONNX-TensorRT 时，模型必须经过 PyTorch ONNX 导出器和 TensorRT ONNX 解析器。

9
00:00:53,635 --> 00:00:57,306
An unsupported op can stop the build.
遇到不支持的算子，构建就可能中止。

10
00:00:57,306 --> 00:01:02,654
Brian: Torch-TensorRT already converts PyTorch ops directly to TensorRT.
Brian：Torch-TensorRT 已经能把 PyTorch 算子直接转换为 TensorRT。

11
00:01:02,654 --> 00:01:07,425
Its usual output still needs libtorch at run time, though.
不过，它通常生成的程序在运行时仍需要 libtorch。

12
00:01:07,425 --> 00:01:17,648
The new route pairs Torch-TensorRT 2.15 with ExecuTorch 1.6, so the robot can run the compiled program without libtorch.
新方案将 Torch-TensorRT 2.15 与 ExecuTorch 1.6 结合，让机器人无需 libtorch 也能运行编译后的程序。

13
00:01:17,648 --> 00:01:23,134
Ava: Where does the split happen if TensorRT can't convert part of a policy?
Ava：如果 TensorRT 无法转换策略中的一部分，程序会怎么分工？

14
00:01:23,134 --> 00:01:27,235
Brian: torch.export first captures a graph of PyTorch ops.
Brian：torch.export 首先捕获 PyTorch 算子的计算图。

15
00:01:27,235 --> 00:01:30,532
TensorRT claims the parts it can convert.
TensorRT 接管它能转换的部分。

16
00:01:30,532 --> 00:01:38,653
ExecuTorch's CUDA backend takes supported parts that TensorRT leaves behind, including preprocessing.
TensorRT 留下的部分，包括预处理，只要受支持，就由 ExecuTorch 的 CUDA 后端接管。

17
00:01:38,653 --> 00:01:43,908
Both backends can run in one program on the same CUDA stream.
两个后端可以在同一个程序、同一条 CUDA 流上运行。

18
00:01:43,908 --> 00:01:48,988
Ava: The article's toy model uses erfinv, which has no TensorRT converter.
Ava：文章中的玩具模型用了 erfinv，而 TensorRT 没有对应的转换器。

19
00:01:48,988 --> 00:01:55,540
So the CUDA backend takes that op, and the compiler reports why it didn't go to TensorRT.
因此 CUDA 后端会接管这个算子，编译器也会报告它为何没有交给 TensorRT。

20
00:01:55,540 --> 00:02:00,602
That's useful when a build doesn't follow the path you expected.
构建结果与预期不符时，这些信息很有用。

21
00:02:00,602 --> 00:02:08,633
Brian: TensorRT builds engines for its parts, while the CUDA backend compiles its part with AOTInductor.
Brian：TensorRT 为接管的部分构建引擎，CUDA 后端则用 AOTInductor 编译自己的部分。

22
00:02:08,633 --> 00:02:11,945
The engines go into a .pte program file.
这些引擎会写入 .pte 程序文件。

23
00:02:11,945 --> 00:02:17,078
The CUDA backend's weights go into a .ptd data file beside it.
CUDA 后端的权重则写入旁边的 .ptd 数据文件。

24
00:02:17,078 --> 00:02:22,294
The CUDA backend needs a CUDA toolkit with nvcc at export time.
导出时，CUDA 后端需要带有 nvcc 的 CUDA 工具包。

25
00:02:22,294 --> 00:02:27,280
Tensors passed between the backends can stay on the GPU.
两个后端之间传递的张量可以留在 GPU 上。

26
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:31,446
Ava: And if neither backend can compile a custom op?
Ava：如果两个后端都无法编译某个自定义算子呢？

27
00:02:31,446 --> 00:02:37,425
Brian: You can write it as a Triton kernel and register it with torch.library.triton_op.
Brian：可以把它写成 Triton 核函数，并通过 torch.library.triton_op 注册。

28
00:02:37,425 --> 00:02:40,821
The CUDA backend compiles it into the program.
CUDA 后端会把它编译进程序。

29
00:02:40,821 --> 00:02:46,412
The robot doesn't need Triton or PyTorch installed to run that program.
机器人运行该程序时，无需安装 Triton 或 PyTorch。

30
00:02:46,412 --> 00:02:53,698
Ava: The article also mentions use_cuda_graphs=True. What does that buy us?
Ava：文章还提到 use_cuda_graphs=True。它有什么用？

31
00:02:53,698 --> 00:02:58,011
Brian: It records each engine's GPU work once as a CUDA graph.
Brian：它会把每个引擎的 GPU 工作录制一次，形成 CUDA 图。

32
00:02:58,011 --> 00:03:04,320
Later calls replay that work with a single launch, making each call cheaper.
后续调用只需启动一次就能重放这些工作，降低每次调用的开销。

33
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:06,010
Ava: What changes at deployment?
Ava：部署时有什么变化？

34
00:03:06,010 --> 00:03:11,366
A robot shouldn't have to load the full training framework just to run a policy.
机器人运行策略时，不该还要加载整个训练框架。

35
00:03:11,366 --> 00:03:20,958
Brian: PyTorch is needed for compilation, but the compiled program runs through the smaller ExecuTorch runtime.
Brian：编译需要 PyTorch，但编译后的程序由更轻量的 ExecuTorch 运行时执行。

36
00:03:20,958 --> 00:03:28,153
It can run from C++ or from Python using NumPy arrays without importing torch.
它既能通过 C++ 运行，也能在 Python 中使用 NumPy 数组运行，无需导入 torch。

37
00:03:28,153 --> 00:03:35,992
On the Orin Nano, the article measured about 2.2 s and 550 MB just to import PyTorch.
文章测得，在 Orin Nano 上，仅导入 PyTorch 就约需 2.2 秒和 550 MB 内存。

38
00:03:35,992 --> 00:03:41,803
The prebuilt wheels target CUDA 13.2 on Linux x86-64 and Arm64.
预编译的 wheel 包面向 Linux x86-64 和 Arm64 平台上的 CUDA 13.2。

39
00:03:41,803 --> 00:03:46,396
On Jetson, that requires JetPack 7.2 or newer.
在 Jetson 上，这要求 JetPack 7.2 或更新版本。

40
00:03:46,396 --> 00:03:53,705
Ava: There's a smaller run-time install, too: about 4.6 GB instead of 11 GB for the full install.
Ava：还有一个更小的运行时安装包：约 4.6 GB，完整安装包则是 11 GB。

41
00:03:53,705 --> 00:04:08,514
If a camera frame is already on the GPU and you export with device inputs and outputs, the C++ app can pass its GPU pointer directly and write actions to an output buffer on the GPU.
如果相机画面已在 GPU 上，且导出时指定设备端输入输出，C++ 应用就能直接传入 GPU 指针，并将动作写入 GPU 上的输出缓冲区。

42
00:04:08,514 --> 00:04:15,308
Brian: The performance test used four LeRobot policies on a Jetson Orin Nano Super with 8 GB of memory.
Brian：性能测试在一台配备 8 GB 内存的 Jetson Orin Nano Super 上，使用了四种 LeRobot 策略。

43
00:04:15,308 --> 00:04:20,544
Each route used the same trained weights and inputs, with no quantization.
各方案使用相同的训练权重和输入，均未量化。

44
00:04:20,544 --> 00:04:29,528
The tables measure time per action chunk and the memory held by the running process, counting CPU and GPU memory together.
表格统计每个动作块的耗时，以及运行进程占用的内存；内存包括 CPU 和 GPU 两部分。

45
00:04:29,528 --> 00:04:46,826
Ava: For ACT, ExecuTorch-TensorRT took 26 ms per chunk, versus 25 ms for ONNX-TensorRT and 48 ms for PyTorch eager.
Ava：对 ACT，ExecuTorch-TensorRT 每块耗时 26 毫秒，ONNX-TensorRT 为 25 毫秒，PyTorch 即时执行模式为 48 毫秒。

46
00:04:46,826 --> 00:05:00,070
For SmolVLA, it took 120 ms, versus 121 ms for ONNX-TensorRT and 765 ms for eager.
对 SmolVLA，三者分别为 120 毫秒、121 毫秒和 765 毫秒。

47
00:05:00,070 --> 00:05:04,900
Brian: The larger policies show the memory advantage.
Brian：更大的策略体现出内存优势。

48
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:12,355
pi0.5 took 467 ms per chunk and held 5538 MiB with ExecuTorch-TensorRT.
pi0.5 使用 ExecuTorch-TensorRT 时，每块耗时 467 毫秒，占用 5538 MiB 内存。

49
00:05:12,355 --> 00:05:16,975
ONNX-TensorRT took 452 ms and held 5429 MiB.
ONNX-TensorRT 耗时 452 毫秒，占用 5429 MiB 内存。

50
00:05:16,975 --> 00:05:29,820
PyTorch eager, torch.compile, and Torch-TensorRT inside PyTorch all ran out of memory for that policy on the Orin Nano.
在 Orin Nano 上运行该策略时，PyTorch 即时执行模式、torch.compile，以及在 PyTorch 中使用的 Torch-TensorRT，都因内存不足而失败。

51
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:39,862
Ava: So the Orin Nano result is close to the ONNX route across all four policies: within 4% in chunk time and process memory.
Ava：Orin Nano 在四项策略上的结果都接近 ONNX 方案：每块处理时间和进程内存占用的差距都在 4% 以内。

52
00:05:39,862 --> 00:05:42,890
How were those numbers measured?
这些数据是怎么测出来的？

53
00:05:42,890 --> 00:05:48,905
Brian: Time is the median of three runs of 100 chunks, after 20 warm-up chunks.
Brian：时间数据取三轮测试的中位数；每轮先预热 20 块，再处理 100 块。

54
00:05:48,905 --> 00:05:54,669
Memory is the median of three runs over the last 30 s of a 120 s run.
内存数据取三轮 120 秒测试中各轮最后 30 秒的中位数。

55
00:05:54,669 --> 00:05:58,344
Files the process only reads aren't counted.
进程只读取的文件不计入内存占用。

56
00:05:58,344 --> 00:06:07,048
The TensorRT routes and torch.compile replay CUDA graphs, with maximum power and a locked GPU clock.
TensorRT 方案和 torch.compile 都会重放 CUDA 图；测试时设为最高功耗模式，并锁定 GPU 时钟频率。

57
00:06:07,048 --> 00:06:11,674
Ava: They also tested a Jetson AGX Thor.
Ava：他们还测试了 Jetson AGX Thor。

58
00:06:11,674 --> 00:06:21,189
For pi0.5, ExecuTorch-TensorRT took 80.5 ms per chunk and held 5617 MiB.
运行 pi0.5 时，ExecuTorch-TensorRT 每块耗时 80.5 ms，占用 5617 MiB 内存。

59
00:06:21,189 --> 00:06:27,136
ONNX-TensorRT took 86.1 ms and held 5495 MiB.
ONNX-TensorRT 耗时 86.1 ms，占用 5495 MiB 内存。

60
00:06:27,136 --> 00:06:37,398
The article says the compiled routes had similar performance on that board.
文章称，这块板子上两种编译方案的性能相近。

61
00:06:37,398 --> 00:06:41,199
Brian: There is a build-time constraint on the smaller board.
Brian：较小的板子在构建时有个限制。

62
00:06:41,199 --> 00:06:52,460
A TensorRT engine is built for one kind of GPU, and building the entire 3.6-billion-parameter policy at once needs more memory than the 8 GB Orin Nano has.
TensorRT 引擎针对特定类型的 GPU 构建，而一次性构建整个 36 亿参数的策略，所需内存超过了 8 GB Orin Nano 的容量。

63
00:06:52,460 --> 00:06:58,362
Ava: So pi0.5 and GR00T 1.7 were split into smaller programs.
Ava：所以 pi0.5 和 GR00T 1.7 被拆成了更小的程序。

64
00:06:58,362 --> 00:07:04,686
Each was built in its own process with only its own weights.
每个程序都在独立进程中构建，只加载自己的权重。

65
00:07:04,686 --> 00:07:17,578
The denoising step then runs 10 times for pi0.5 and 4 times for GR00T, with tensors passed between programs on the GPU.
随后，pi0.5 的去噪步骤运行 10 次，GR00T 运行 4 次；张量在 GPU 上的程序之间传递。

66
00:07:17,578 --> 00:07:24,130
Brian: At run time, ExecuTorch's shared GPU memory allocator also helps the engines fit.
Brian：运行时，ExecuTorch 的共享 GPU 内存分配器也有助于装下这些引擎。

67
00:07:24,130 --> 00:07:31,032
The article says pi0.5's second engine wouldn't load on the Orin Nano without it.
文章称，没有它，pi0.5 的第二个引擎就无法在 Orin Nano 上加载。

68
00:07:31,032 --> 00:07:35,182
Ava: A robot may run several policies on one GPU.
Ava：一个机器人可能在同一块 GPU 上运行多项策略。

69
00:07:35,182 --> 00:07:43,671
If one process loads the same program twice, the engines can stay in GPU memory just once.
如果同一进程两次加载同一个程序，引擎在 GPU 显存中只需保留一份。

70
00:07:43,671 --> 00:07:50,246
On the Orin Nano, that second load took 76 MiB instead of 805 MiB.
在 Orin Nano 上，第二次加载只占 76 MiB，而不是 805 MiB。

71
00:07:50,246 --> 00:07:52,059
Brian: Sharing compute is harder.
Brian：共享计算资源就更难了。

72
00:07:52,059 --> 00:08:00,076
A CUDA green context can give each policy a fixed set of streaming multiprocessors, with its own stream and thread.
CUDA green context（绿色上下文）可以给每项策略分配固定数量的流式多处理器，并让它们各自使用独立的流和线程。

73
00:08:00,076 --> 00:08:09,628
Memory bandwidth is still shared, and an engine can fail if its green context has too few streaming multiprocessors for its kernels.
但内存带宽仍是共享的；如果绿色上下文分到的流式多处理器太少，引擎的内核可能无法运行。

74
00:08:09,628 --> 00:08:19,217
Ava: So the useful picture is a small run-time program, TensorRT engines where they fit, and a CUDA backend for supported parts they can't take.
Ava：可以这样理解：用一个小型运行时程序，在适合的地方使用 TensorRT 引擎，引擎处理不了但受支持的部分则交给 CUDA 后端。

75
00:08:19,217 --> 00:08:25,914
The Orin Nano measurements show why both speed and process memory matter for these policies.
Orin Nano 的测量结果说明，对这些策略来说，速度和进程内存占用都很重要。

76
00:08:25,914 --> 00:08:30,767
Brian: And big policies still need careful building on an 8 GB board.
Brian：而在 8 GB 的板子上，大型策略仍需精心构建。

77
00:08:30,767 --> 00:08:34,952
That's it for this episode. Thanks for listening.
这期节目就到这里。感谢收听。
